items=[('island-study','01 / Island','Chocolate oak and shaped pale stone','Framed panels, substantial corner posts and a shaped edge. Kept at 2.4 × 1.0 m for this study. The hob is a placeholder; its type and position are not selected.'),('stool-study','02 / Stools','Curved timber backs and solid seats','Custom models based on your new reference: broad curved backs, shaped wood seats, splayed legs and foot rails. Seat height is about 670 mm. These are not exact retail models.'),('cabinet-study','03 / Cabinets and sink','Ceiling-height cabinets and a concealed pantry door','The sink window has no surrounding cupboards. The tall fridge and pantry bank meet the 3.2 m test ceiling. A plain corner return replaces the narrow framed panels. The pantry entrance has aligned cabinet panels, matching pulls and no room-door architrave.'),('pendant-study','04 / Lighting','Milk-glass pendant direction','Two conical shades with warm bronze fittings. The shape follows selected option 4B. The final fitting and lighting levels remain to be checked.'),('kitchen-room','05 / Kitchen','The pieces in the selected space','Option D kitchen with the pantry entrance concealed in the cabinet wall at right. The return cabinets are 350 mm deep, leaving about 1.05 m beside the island. The window wall stays open above the worktop. Pale oak herringbone follows your floor reference.'),('pantry-utility','06 / Pantry','Enclosed storage with a utility connection','View from the 1.8 × 2.5 m pantry through its open connecting door. A separate cupboard-style door connects the pantry directly to the kitchen. The utility keeps its laundry appliances and folding counter.')]
for name,*_ in items:shutil.copy2(O/(name+'.png'),I/(name+'.png'))
figs=''.join(f'<article id="{n}"><a href="kitchen-renders/{n}.png" target="_blank"><img src="kitchen-renders/{n}.png" alt="{escape(t)}" width="1500" height="{1125 if k<4 else 1000}" {"loading=lazy" if k>1 else ""}></a><div class="caption"><span>{escape(label)}</span><h2>{escape(t)}</h2><p>{escape(desc)}</p></div></article>' for k,(n,label,t,desc) in enumerate(items))
refs=''.join(f'<a href="references/{n}.png" target="_blank">{title}</a>' for n,title in [('stool','Stools'),('island-floor','Island and floor'),('cabinetry','Cabinetry'),('sink-counter','Sink and counter')])
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>L-house · Kitchen furniture study</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f3f0e8;color:#293f32;font:16px/1.55 system-ui}header,main,footer{max-width:1380px;margin:auto;padding:32px}header{padding-top:46px}h1{font:normal clamp(34px,4.5vw,54px)/1.1 Georgia,serif;margin:15px 0 20px}h2{font:normal 27px/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:8px 0 14px}p{max-width:850px}a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:4px}nav{display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:24px}.eyebrow,.caption span{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase}.summary{padding:20px 24px;background:#284836;color:#fffdf7;margin-top:24px}.summary p{margin:4px 0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:28px}article{background:#fffdf7;border:1px solid #d4d6ca;min-width:0}article img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.caption{padding:22px}.caption p{margin-bottom:0}.note{padding:22px;background:#ede1c9;margin-top:30px}.refs{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap}footer{padding-top:0;font-size:14px}@media(max-width:750px){header,main,footer{padding:20px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:22px}.caption{padding:18px}h2{font-size:25px}}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a87943;outline-offset:4px}</style><header><div class="eyebrow">L-house / Kitchen study / 7 October 2026</div><h1>Warm ivory. Dark oak.<br>Curved timber stools.</h1><p>Four separate furniture previews, followed by two views in the selected kitchen and pantry layout. Open any image to inspect the details.</p><nav><a href="combined.html">Combined rooms →</a><a href="boot-room.html">Selected layout</a><a href="index.html">Earlier selections</a><a href="#kitchen-room">Room views</a></nav><div class="summary"><p><strong>Enclosed pantry with two connections.</strong> The kitchen door and utility door are both retained.</p></div></header><main><div class="grid">FIGURES</div><div class="note"><h2>What this study settles</h2><p>The furniture forms and finish direction. It does not settle the final kitchen specification. Keep the current island size while testing more space behind occupied stools; the larger 3.2 × 1.4 m island in the reference has not been adopted.</p><p>Next layout checks: space behind occupied stools, appliance use, pantry door swing and access to the high cupboards. The island-to-cabinet gap is about 1.05 m with doors closed. The breakfast cupboard remains to be placed. The glass divider and full daylight comparison belong to the next room-layout pass. The first-floor level has not yet been coordinated with the taller ceiling.</p></div><h2 style="margin-top:32px">Your latest references</h2><div class="refs">REFERENCES</div><p>The image labels identify reference products. No product or asset was purchased. The stronger splashback veining and oak-lined breakfast cupboard are retained as references for the next cabinet layout pass.</p></main><footer><p>Actual Blender/Cycles renders from a separate study file. The approved living-room source remains unchanged. Lighting is for visual comparison, not a daylight calculation.</p></footer></html>'''.replace('FIGURES',figs).replace('REFERENCES',refs)
(D/'renders.html').write_text(page)
